WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.040
Let's dress up our Russian skills today with everyday clothing words that help you talk about what you're wearing right now. I'm Olya, and this is Привет, Русский, episode 65. Our word of the day is Adiertha. Adiertha, sit slowly with me, or Diertha, now at normal speed Adiertha. It means clothes or clothing. Think of a Diertha like Adisha you dye your clothes different colors. Here's a simple sentence.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:54.880
У меня есть новая Adiertha, that means I have new clothes. Repeat after me, Adiertha. Now let's build more vocabulary around clothes. The Russian word for shirt is rubashka. Rubashka, repeat after me, rubashka. It sounds like rubashka. Imagine a ruster wearing a bashful shirt. Here is a simple sentence. I'll find a new rubashka. That means I am wearing a blue shirt. Repeat after me, rubashka, rubashka. Next comes breuki, breuki. Repeat after me, breuki.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:24.860
This means trousers or pants. Think of breuki, trousers you wear while brewing tea. Here is a simple sentence. Мои брюки черные, that means my trousers are black. Repeat after me, breuki, breuki. Address is platia, platia. Repeat after me, platia. It sounds like platia, a plate of pretty fabric. Here is a simple sentence. Девочка носит красивая platia. That means the girl is wearing a beautiful dress. Repeat after me.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:43.640
Платия, платия. Footwear or shoes is oboof, oboof. Repeat after me, oboof. Say oboof, like oboof, boots that make you boogie. Here is a simple sentence. Моя oboof удобная. That means my shoes are comfortable. Repeat after me, oboof, oboof.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:50.240
Сокс are носки, носки. Repeat after me, носки, носки. They hold the key to warm toes.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:59.600
Here is a simple sentence. Я покупаю теплые носки. That means I am buying warm socks. Repeat after me, носки, носки.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:07.180
А джакет из куртка. Куртка. Репит after me. Куртка. Куртка. А джакет you wear to court or just to stay warm.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:13.440
Here is a simple sentence. Зимой я надеваю куртку. That means in winter I put on a jacket.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:22.720
Репит after me. Куртка. Куртка. А hat or cap is шапка. Шапка. Репит after me. Шапка. It sounds like shape cap, a shape like cap.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:30.240
Here is a simple sentence. Надень шапку на голову. That means put a hat on your head. Repeat after me. Шапка. Шапка.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:38.280
Бутс or shoes are batинки. Batинки. Repeat after me. Batинки. Batинки. Тени бутстат метью тенни-тенни-степс.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:46.100
Here is a simple sentence. Batинки на ногах. That means buts are on my feet. Repeat after me. Batинки. Batинки.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:53.540
Ремемор большая from before. It means big. Now for a grammar bite. In Russian adjectives change to match the noun.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:03:01.760
Look at these examples with our new words. Синие рубашка means blue shirt. The ending on sin matches the feminine word рубашка.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:08.380
Чёрное брюки means black trousers. The ending on chorna matches the plural word брюки.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:15.420
Удобная обувь means comfortable footwear. The ending on uдобная matches the feminine word oboe.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:21.740
Unlike indrish, Russian adjectives agree with the noun. Once you spot the pattern, it feels natural.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:29.980
There is something really cool about one of today's words. Куртка began in French as a jacket and entered Russian in the 18th century.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:38.240
When French fashion words arrived in big numbers. The surprise is that Russian word means clothing terms from French during Peter the Great's era.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:44.660
Пикчер of French courtier handed you a courteca jacket. That picture locks the sound in your mind.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:52.820
Russian swear a шапка, and warm felt boots in winter, because the cold is serious. Bright scarves and gloves make popular gifts.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:04:05.340
Children hear their babushka say надень шапку, which means boot on your hat. For the practice challenge kids can draw themselves wearing three new items and label them рубашка брюки and шапка.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:11.140
Адальс can look in the wardrobe and say out loud, у меня есть, plus, 3 clothing words they see.

